Description: analyzer findings (NuDanOS code-quality lint)
 NULL terminators of run_netplug_bg's variable arguments passed as
 (char *) NULL; do_log starts its va_list after the early return, so every
 va_start has its va_end; the script's log line is built with bounded
 snprintf instead of strncpy/strncat with the buffer size as bound (which
 could write past the end); sizeof(*tb) and sizeof(*ifa) where the code
 meant the element and the struct, not a pointer (the same size on amd64);
 calloc arguments in order; signed/unsigned comparisons with explicit casts
 where the value cannot be negative; const where pointers are only read;
 (void) for callback-signature parameters; narrower variable scopes; quoted
 arguments in the netplug script; reasoned cppcheck suppressions where it
 cannot see a callback or the header's users.
Author: NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
